<report>
<title>Sample size for matched case-control study</title>

<p>case-control correlation = <inu>corr</inu><br />
probability of exposure in controls = <inu>pc</inu><br />
odds ratio = <inu>odds</inu><br />
controls per case subject = <inu>cpc</inu><br />
alpha = <inu>alpha</inu><br />
power = <inu>power</inu></p>
<block name="lower">

<p><warn>NB. Assuming power from lower tail is negligible.</warn></p>
</block>
<block name="illegal">
<p>Illegal odds ratio</p>
</block>

<p>Estimated minimum sample size (cases required) = <in>size</in></p>
<block name="reduction">

<p>Reduction in sample size, relative to paired design,<br />
when using <in>controls</in> controls per case = <in>reduction</in></p>
</block>
<block name="assumptions">

<p><warn>NB:Assumptions of this calculation may cause over estimation of sample size when power is low.  However, true power associated with <in>cases</in> cases will be no less than <in>no_less</in> and no greater than <in>no_greater</in>.</warn></p>
</block>
</report>
